 "anomalies": [
  "F12 carries a strong 15734.3 Hz tone (~+13 dB, the NTSC horizontal line rate) - the master was transferred through video-based digital audio (PCM adaptor / VHS or U-matic). This is the likeliest source of its 51 ppm speed error.",
  "120 Hz mains hum is present in all three tracks, wandering 119.98-120.26 Hz. Because it wanders it cannot be used to calibrate transfer speed; the carrier grid can.",
  "F10 has no round-number grid at all and its two pair members drift independently: its beats are not constant. F12/F15 are frequency-stable to a part in 10^5 or better.",
  "F15's deep-section layer (300.0/304.8/503.9/511.2/599.3/606.6/800.0/807.3 Hz) is exact to 0.1 ppm yet sits at strange non-round frequencies with a repeated 7.3 Hz split. Its provenance differs from everything else measured.",
  "The F12 and F15 exit signals use the identical tone set {467,483,568,592,608,632} with the channels mirrored - strong evidence of a shared library of stock 'exit' cues."
 ],
