 "folklore_comparison": {
  "premise": "Measured first, compared second. Folklore claims ~100/104-style pairs and multi-layer stacks at 100/200/250/300 Hz with ~1.5/4/16 Hz beats.",
  "agrees": [
   "100/104 with a 4 Hz beat: F10 pair A measures 99.98/104.03, beat 4.05. Essentially exact.",
   "Carriers at 100/200/250/300: F12 has precisely these centres (100+/-0.75, 200+/-2, 250+/-2, 300+/-2) - exactly, once the 51 ppm transfer error is removed.",
   "Beats of 1.5 and 4 Hz: F12's 100-pair is 1.500 and all three of 200/250/300 are 4.000.",
   "A 16 Hz beat exists: confirmed in both F12 and F15."
  ],
  "disagrees": [
   "16 Hz is in the WRONG PLACE. Not a body layer: it appears only in the 90-160 s exit signal, on carriers centred at 475 and 600 Hz, alongside a 64 Hz pair the folklore never mentions.",
   "The entire 10 Hz layer is missing from the folklore: carriers 400/500/600 with 10.0 Hz beats run for 19 minutes of F12 and reappear in F15.",
   "The 50 Hz cluster is missing: a centred mono 50.0 Hz anchor plus 0.25/0.5/0.75 Hz monaural AND binaural beats runs the full length of F12 and F15.",
   "Channel polarity is ignored by folklore. F12 is L-high throughout; F15 deliberately flips to R-high for its main body, reversing every beat sign.",
   "'Fixed nice numbers' is false for F10: carriers are not round, beats drift 4.12 -> 3.89 over the session, and its three pairs target 4 Hz but land on 4.05, 3.85 and -3.70. Regenerating F10 from folklore numbers yields something measurably different.",
   "F15's deep section is absent from folklore entirely: 4.8 and 7.3 Hz beats on 300/500/600/800 Hz carriers, for 19 of its 40 minutes."
  ]
 },
 "confidence_notes": {
  "high": "All F12/F15 carrier frequencies and beats (coherent 600 s FFTs, tone residuals <0.001 Hz, every beat confirmed by envelope demodulation). The F12 51 ppm speed error (18 tones agreeing to +/-0.5 ppm). The F12 mono-50 Hz finding (L/R phase locked -10 +/- 6 deg across 30 blocks, plus three-way envelope confirmation).",
  "good": "F10's three pairs and drift trajectories. The ~0.5 Hz AM on F10 pair B (sidebands 19 dB down, consistent across many blocks). Layer on/off times, good to about +/-30 s given fade-ins and the 60 s block grid.",
  "lower": [
   "Levels are section medians; individual carriers move +/-6 dB during fades.",
   "The bed's level_rel_carriers uses a crude +/-2 Hz tonal notch, reliable only to a few dB. F10's is inflated because the wide median filter smears low-frequency carrier energy into the floor estimate below ~300 Hz. Above 1 kHz the bed numbers are clean.",
   "F15's 175/179 and 262/266 pairs are low-level and short-lived; frequencies scatter +/-0.01 Hz, so membership in the exact-grid family is undetermined.",
   "The F15 deep layer's generating rule is unknown. Ratios, harmonic relations and speed-rescalings all fail; intermodulation is ruled out because nothing in that section is loud enough to produce products only 25 dB below itself. Frequencies are certain; their meaning is not.",
   "The F12/F15 exit 64 Hz pair (568/632) is inferred from the centre+/-half-beat pattern that fits {467,483}=475-/+8 and {592,608}=600-/+8, giving 568/632=600-/+32. Channel assignment is consistent and F15 mirrors it exactly, but 64 Hz is above the binaural fusion limit, so 'pair' here is a structural claim, not a perceptual one."
  ]
 }
